@how own mechanism: scrub each clause so it references only the layer’s own mechanisms, blockers, exports, and guarantees; move projections into the appropriate futon or retire them until evidence exists. (source: this pattern's ! conclusion line; L9 rationale-backfill, zai-1, 2026-09-05)

! conclusion: 
  scrub each clause so it references only the layer’s own mechanisms,
  blockers, exports, and guarantees; move projections into the appropriate futon
  or retire them until evidence exists.

  + context: To ensure your devmaps accurately describe a layer's mechanisms, avoid referencing unrelated projections that dilute clarity.

  + IF:
    devmaps are supposed to describe the guarantees and mechanisms intrinsic to a
    layer.

  + HOWEVER:
    entries often drift into upstream/downstream speculation (agents,
    policies, future futons), diluting responsibility boundaries.

  + THEN:
    scrub each clause so it references only the layer’s own mechanisms,
    blockers, exports, and guarantees; move projections into the appropriate futon
    or retire them until evidence exists.

  + BECAUSE:
    sharp scope makes layers composable and keeps stack blockers
    observable.

    + EVIDENCE:
      evidence[library/devmap-coherence/prototype-alignment-bridge.flexiarg:1]

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Apply this check to FUTON1–4 devmaps; annotate clauses that mention external futons without bridges.]
